      "error_message": "App starts but shows blank white canvas — no UI visible after loading screen",
      "file": "src/main/index.js, src/main/ipc-handlers.js",
      "root_cause": "IPC handlers were registered AFTER the window loaded and started the renderer. The sequence was: (1) createWindow() called, (2) window.loadURL() immediately loads renderer, (3) renderer mounts and calls window.api.readConfig() in useIpcEvents.js, (4) IPC handler hasn't been registered yet! → all IPC calls fail silently → nothing renders. Additionally, mainWindow parameter was passed to handlers before being set, so handlers couldn't send events back to renderer.",
      "fix": "1. Moved handler registration to BEFORE createWindow() in app.whenReady(). 2. Changed handler signature from registerIpcHandlers(downloadManager, mainWindow, logger) to registerIpcHandlers(downloadManager, logger, getMainWindow) where getMainWindow returns the global mainWindow reference. 3. Created sendToRenderer() helper that safely calls getMainWindow() before sending IPC events. 4. Replaced all mainWindow.webContents.send() calls with sendToRenderer().",
      "tags": [
        "ipc-initialization",
        "window-lifecycle",
        "render-blank-screen",
        "race-condition"
